        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nNow I'll fix the benchmark file. The key issues are:\n\n1. The `SetBytesProcessed` function currently sets both items and bytes to the same value (bytes_processed)\n2. For booleans, it uses `sizeof(typename ParquetType::c_type)` which is 1 byte, but booleans are bit-packed (1 bit per value)\n3. For Float16LogicalType, it should use 2 bytes per item, not sizeof(c_type)\n\nLet me create the fix:\n\n",
          "time": {
            "start": 1781824169190,
            "end": 1781824169210
          },
          "id": "prt_edcff24e6001r44ENZYXmhT9zD",
          "sessionID": "ses_12301ff8bffepGRXNraGw2b8eW",
