          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nExcellent! The changes look good. Let me create a summary document of what was changed:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the Parquet Arrow benchmark suite to correctly report performance metrics. The key changes made to `/workspace/cpp/src/parquet/arrow/reader_writer_benchmark.cc` are:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **Added include for bit_util.h** (line 41):\n   - Needed for the `BytesForBits` function to calculate bit-packed boolean storage\n\n2. **Added helper functions** (lines 101-121):\n   - `GetBytesPerItem<ParquetType>()`: Returns bytes per item for each type (0 for booleans, 2 for Float16, sizeof(c_type) for others)\n   - `CalculateBytesProcessed<ParquetType>(num_items)`: Calculates total bytes using proper storage size for each type\n\n3. **Renamed and fixed `SetBytesProcessed` to `SetMetricsProcessed`** (lines 130-144):\n   - Now correctly sets `items_processed` separately from `bytes_processed`\n   - For **BooleanType**: Uses `arrow::bit_util::BytesForBits()` to calculate bit-packed storage (1 bit per value)\n   - For **Float16LogicalType**: Uses 2 bytes per item (not sizeof(c_type))\n   - For other types: Uses `sizeof(c_type)` bytes per item\n\n4. **Updated all benchmark functions** to use the new metric calculation:\n   - `BM_WriteColumn`: Now calls `SetMetricsProcessed` instead of `SetBytesProcessed`\n   - `BM_ReadColumn`: Now passes correct byte count via `CalculateBytesProcessed`\n   - `BM_ReadColumnPlain`: Now passes correct byte count via `CalculateBytesProcessed`\n   - `BM_ReadIndividualRowGroups`, `BM_ReadMultipleRowGroups`, `BM_ReadMultipleRowGroupsGenerator`: All updated to use `SetMetricsProcessed`\n\n### Impact:\n\n- **Boolean benchmarks** will now show a much lower byte rate (~1/8th of the item count) reflecting true bit-packed storage\n- **Float16 benchmarks** will correctly report 2 bytes per item instead of sizeof(uint16_t)\n- **All other types** (Int32, Int64, Double) continue to work correctly with proper byte counts\n- **Items per second** and **bytes per second** are now reported as separate, accurate metrics\n- The benchmark output will now allow accurate comparison of write and read speeds across different data types",
